/* ===== LESSON STANDARD v2 (Oct 14, 2026). Every new or rewritten lesson follows this; v2 lessons carry v:2. =====
   Reader: someone trying to QUIT PORN, not a scientist. Each lesson does three jobs for ONE idea: understand the habit,
   understand the science (plain words), know how to quit (a concrete move).
   Shape: ask (the one question the lesson answers; shown on the cover and again on Done) and key (the answer).
     hook (Quick+Full)   a moment he recognizes; headline IS the question, no answer yet
     predict (Full)      guess first: 4 beliefs people really hold, one right (choose with a) or a guess slider
     answer (Quick+Full) what is going on in the habit, plain words
     proof x1-2 (Full)   the science as a short plain story + so: "What this means for you" (bridge to porn/quitting)
     move (Quick+Full)   what to do, concrete, doable tonight
     check (Quick+Full)  last card: a realistic moment, 4 real moves, ONE best answer (a)
   Then Done (question + "The answer" + private note np), Put it to work (act), Practiced.
   Questions must check or apply this lesson's idea. NO polls ("Tap one", "which is you"), NO study-detail or
   definition questions, NO "not sure / not ready / none" options, NO joke distractors, NO pointers to other lessons.
   Replies open with a verdict, teach in under 40 words, never shame. Answers stay switchable (tap any choice to read its
   comment). Recall (rc, shown in the next lesson) applies the idea to a NEW scenario, with a comment per choice (cr);
   never asks about a study. Claims match sources; limits go in scope ("Behind this").
   Plain words, no jargon in headlines, no contractions, no hedging in card copy. Lint: node lint_lessons.js */
